    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (the `AcceptanceTest` class holds the only `@Test` methods; `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table, following the codebase's existing conventions:\n\n1. **`util/LocalityResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 a pure lookup function mirroring `AddressNormalizer`. It resolves `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD` via an exact-match table, returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other (or null) city \u2014 matching the test's ground-truth `region()` helper semantics.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the response JSON.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression wiring `locality` to `LocalityResolver.resolve(owner.getCity())`, consistent with the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\nResult: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both the known-city (`Sydney`\u2192`NSW`) and unknown-city (`UNKNOWN`) acceptance tests are green.",
